n",["Date","2026-08-21T00:00:00.000Z"],"Camille Buonomo",false,"import Presentation from \"../../components/Presentation.astro\";\nimport Slide from \"../../components/Slide.astro\";\n\n\u003CPresentation>\n\n\u003CSlide>\n\n# My First Presentation\n\nCamille Buonomo\n\n\u003C/Slide>\n\n\u003CSlide>\n\n# Motivation\n\nThis is the motivation.\n\n\u003C/Slide>\n\n\u003CSlide>\n\n# Method\n\nThis is the method.\n\n\u003C/Slide>\n\n\u003CSlide>\n\n# Results\n\nThese are the results.\n\n\u003C/Slide>\n\n\u003CSlide>\n\n# My First Presentation\n\nCamille Buonomo\n\n\u003C/Slide>\n\n\u003CSlide>\n\n# Motivation\n\nThis is the motivation.\n\n\u003C/Slide>\n\n\u003CSlide>\n\n# Method\n\nThis is the method.\n\n\u003C/Slide>\n\n\u003CSlide>\n\n# Results\n\nThese are the results.\n\n\u003C/Slide>\n\n\u003CSlide>\n\n# My First Presentation\n\nCamille Buonomo\n\n\u003C/Slide>\n\n\u003CSlide>\n\n# Motivation\n\nThis is the motivation.\n\n\u003C/Slide>\n\n\u003CSlide>\n\n# Method\n\nThis is the method.\n\n\u003C/Slide>\n\n\u003CSlide>\n\n# Results\n\nThese are the results.\n\n\u003C/Slide>\n\n\u003CSlide>\n\n# My First Presentation\n\nCamille Buonomo\n\n\u003C/Slide>\n\n\u003CSlide>\n\n# Motivation\n\nThis is the motivation.\n\n\u003C/Slide>\n\n\u003CSlide>\n\n# Method\n\nThis is the method.\n\n\u003C/Slide>\n\n\u003CSlide>\n\n# Results\n\nThese are the results.\n\n\u003C/Slide>\n\n\u003CSlide>\n\n# My First Presentation\n\nCamille Buonomo\n\n\u003C/Slide>\n\n\u003CSlide>\n\n# Motivation\n\nThis is the motivation.\n\n\u003C/Slide>\n\n\u003CSlide>\n\n# Method\n\nThis is the method.\n\n\u003C/Slide>\n\n\u003CSlide>\n\n# Results\n\nThese are the results.\n\n\u003C/Slide>\n\n\u003C/Presentation>","src/content/presentations/test.mdx","d9a9e40c465abb0d",true,"publications",["Map",25,26,11,40,259,260],"explicit-flows-for-implicit-surfaces",{"id":25,"data":27,"body":37,"filePath":38,"digest":39,"deferredRender":22},{"title":28,"authors":29,"year":32,"venue":33,"doi":34,"hal":35,"image":36},"Explicit Flows for Implicit Surfaces",[17,30,31],"Julie Digne","Raphaëlle Chaine",2026,"ACM Transactions on Graphics","10.1145/3811331","hal-05622054","/images/publications/explicit-flows/explicit-flows-for-implicit-surfaces.png","import PlyVideo from \"../../components/PlyVideo.astro\";\n\n\n\u003Cdiv style=\"display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; gap: 3rem; font-size: 2.5rem; margin: 1.5rem 0;\">\n  \u003Ca\n    href=\"https://github.com/camillebnm/explicit_flows_for_implicit_surfaces\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\n    style=\"color: #58a6ff; font-weight: 600;\"\n  >Code\u003C/a>\n\n  \u003Ca\n    href=\"/papers/buonomo26.pdf\"\n    style=\"color: #e07a5f; font-weight: 600;\"\n  >Paper\u003C/a>\n\u003C/div>\n\n\n\n\u003Ciframe\n  width=\"100%\"\n  height=\"500\"\n  src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/I1tN22cfa1c\"\n  title=\"Video\"\n  frameborder=\"0\"\n  allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\"\n  allowfullscreen\n>\u003C/iframe>\n\n## Abstract\n\nShape deformation for morphing or editing purposes is a central challenge in Computer Graphics. While numerous methods exist, few allow for the explicit evaluation of the deformation at arbitrary times and locations without relying on intricate advection or interpolation schemes. We propose a method that provides an explicit expression of the deformation parameterized as a flow for continuously deforming implicitly defined shapes. Our approach leverages invertible neural networks to guarantee that the deformation is a valid flow while providing differential quantities useful for geometric regularization. We demonstrate applications to shape morphing with and without landmarks, shape editing, and pairwise-to-any morphing, where pairwise morphings to a canonical shape can be composed to obtain transformations between arbitrary pairs of shapes.\n\n## Example\n\n\u003Cdiv class=\"ply-video-row\">\n\n  \u003CPlyVide